m horizon  +0
# Model a non-zero one-way light time on the 2<->3 link.  OWLT only widens
# LTP's computed timers (it does not actually delay loopback packets), and
# this test needs it: after the relay spends the sender's checkpoint budget,
# the sender holds the export session open for roughly maxretries x the
# checkpoint timer before giving up.  With OWLT 0 that window is ~2s -- too
# short for the relay to observe exhaustion and deliver the held completing
# report, so on slower runners the session is cancelled first and BP
# re-forwards (a false duplicate).  A realistic OWLT makes the window many
# seconds, so the completing report reliably lands in time on every platform.
a range    +0 +600		2 3   5
a contact  +0 +600		2 2   10000
a contact  +0 +600		3 3   10000
a contact  +0 +600		2 3   10000
a contact  +0 +600		3 2   10000
